       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6000 mg/day. The usual maximum for an adult is 4000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is double the usual maximum of 1000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** At this dose, even with normal liver function, there is a real risk of hepatotoxicity.\n\nHere are some options that may be what you meant:\n1. Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily (3000 mg/day).\n2. Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily (4000 mg/day, the maximum).\n3. Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2600 mg/day).\n\nTell me which one you want, or give me a different dose if I misread the order, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
